# Source

Hallmark, vendored whole. The entry point `skills/hallmark/SKILL.md` is upstream's
own file and is listed below with the rest: this library ships no tezgah-authored
entry point, because Hallmark's SKILL.md is the workflow we run.

- `hallmark` - https://github.com/Nutlope/hallmark at revision
  `7ec868225c6caa040558c321ee0fefa0e73f83a8` (2026-10-22), MIT, Copyright (c)
  2026 Hallmark contributors, made by Together AI. The whole `skills/hallmark/`
  tree: 1 `SKILL.md`, 98 reference pages (48 themes with their pictures, 20
  macrostructures, anatomy, layout, imagery, craft, gates, genres and the rest),
  and 10 zero-dependency Node scripts under `scripts/`.

Nothing is adapted: every file is upstream's bytes at that revision. Hallmark's
own `LICENSE` sits beside this file as upstream ships it.

Checkout for a re-vendor:

    git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/Nutlope/hallmark.git
    cd hallmark && git sparse-checkout set skills/hallmark
    git rev-parse HEAD          # must equal the revision above

Copy `skills/hallmark/` over this directory, replace every sha256 below, and
update the revision here - all in one commit. `tests/test_skills.py`
(`HallmarkVendor`) fails on a file that no longer matches its hash, on a listed
file that is missing, and on a file beside them the table does not list.

